<!DOCTYPE qhelp PUBLIC
  "-//Semmle//qhelp//EN"
  "qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>
<overview>
<p>
Meson, CMake, and qmake setup hooks already enable parallel building for the
standard configure phase. When a derivation also sets
<code>enableParallelBuilding = true;</code>, the attribute is redundant and adds
noise without changing the build.
</p>
<p>
This only holds while the default hook-driven configure phase is still in use.
If the derivation overrides <code>configurePhase</code>, or explicitly disables the
relevant hook with <code>dontUseMesonConfigure</code>,
<code>dontUseCmakeConfigure</code>, or <code>dontUseQmakeConfigure</code>, then an
explicit <code>enableParallelBuilding</code> may still be necessary.
</p>
</overview>

<recommendation>
<p>
Remove <code>enableParallelBuilding = true;</code> from derivations that already
use Meson, CMake, or qmake through the default configure hook. Keep the binding
only when you intentionally bypass or disable that hook.
</p>
</recommendation>

<example>
<p>Problematic — CMake already enables parallel building:</p>
<sample language="nix">
{ stdenv, cmake }:
stdenv.mkDerivation {
  pname = "demo";
  version = "1.0";
  enableParallelBuilding = true;
  nativeBuildInputs = [ cmake ];
}
</sample>
<p>Recommended — rely on the setup hook:</p>
<sample language="nix">
{ stdenv, cmake }:
stdenv.mkDerivation {
  pname = "demo";
  version = "1.0";
  nativeBuildInputs = [ cmake ];
}
</sample>
<p>Safe — custom configure phase, so the explicit opt-in may be needed:</p>
<sample language="nix">
{ stdenv, cmake }:
stdenv.mkDerivation {
  pname = "demo";
  version = "1.0";
  enableParallelBuilding = true;
  nativeBuildInputs = [ cmake ];
  configurePhase = ''
    runHook preConfigure
    cmake -S . -B build
    runHook postConfigure
  '';
}
</sample>
</example>

<references>
<li>
<a href="https://github.com/jtojnar/nixpkgs-hammering/blob/main/explanations/unnecessary-parallel-building.md">
<code>nixpkgs-hammering</code> explanation: <code>unnecessary-parallel-building</code></a>
</li>
<li>
Nixpkgs setup hooks:
<a href="https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/development/tools/build-managers/meson/setup-hook.sh">Meson</a>,
<a href="https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/development/tools/build-managers/cmake/setup-hook.sh">CMake</a>,
<a href="https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/development/libraries/qt-5/hooks/qmake-hook.sh">qmake</a>
</li>
</references>
</qhelp>
